~~~
{}{raw}
<section aria-labelledby="sgd-heading">
<h2 id="sgd-heading">Dynamical stability of SGD</h2>
~~~

We pioneered the dynamical-stability perspective on SGD's implicit regularization to understand why SGD favors some minima over others. Our work connects the dynamical stability of minima to their sharpness and generalization properties.

- *Minima selection through dynamical stability.* [https://papers.nips.cc/paper/8049-how-sgd-selects-the-global-minima-in-over-parameterized-learning-a-dynamical-stability-perspective NeurIPS 2018].
- *SGD noise alignment and flat-minimum selection.* [https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.02628 NeurIPS 2022].
- *Stability-induced implicit regularization and generalization.* [https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17490 ICML 2023].
- *The noise geometry of SGD.* [https://openreview.net/forum?id=F6wmIilZXG TMLR 2026].

For an overview, see my [doc/dynamical-stability.pdf talk slides].

~~~
{}{raw}
</section>
~~~

~~~
{}{raw}
<section aria-labelledby="barron-heading">
<h2 id="barron-heading">Barron spaces and neural-network function spaces</h2>
~~~

We introduced and named Barron spaces for two-layer neural networks, establishing approximation and generalization results within this function-space framework. Our broader work studies how neural networks *efficiently* approximate and learn high-dimensional functions, and how their capabilities differ from kernel and random-feature methods.

- *Barron spaces and flow-induced function spaces: direct and inverse approximation theorems.* [https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.08039 Constructive Approximation 2021].
- *Two-layer neural networks versus linear methods.* [https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.04964 JMLR 2022].
- *Inductive biases in deep convolutional networks.* [https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.08404 NeurIPS 2023].
- *A duality framework linking approximation and estimation.* [https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.05642 AoS 2025].

For an overview, see my [doc/function-space.pdf talk slides].

